<title>UK: DBSA adds 2.5 billion rand to zero-coupon bond.</title>
<headline>DBSA adds 2.5 billion rand to zero-coupon bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was increased</p>
<p>by joint lead managers Hambros Bank and Rand Merchant Bank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DEVELOPMENT BANK OF SOUTHERN AFRICA</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  REPUBLIC OF SOUTH AFRICA</p>
<p> AMT ** 7.5 BLN RAND  COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    31.DEC.27</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  2.75	PAY DATE    11.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.25	LISTING    LUX</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  BAA1/BBB+ DENOMS (K) 5-50-500  SALE LIMITS US.UK/SA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  S.A	 TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.125     PRAECIPUUM  0.10</p>
<p> NOTES	SENIOR, UNSECURED AND UNSUBORDINATED</p>
<p>	    **ORIGINAL 5.0 BLN RAND BOND LAUNCHED ON JULY 25,</p>
<p>INCREASED</p>
<p>		BY 2.5 BLN RAND</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
